; A closed subset of ECMAScript as data: identifiers, the AST, a printer and a
; scope checker. Nothing here knows the Loop IR, so a second producer needs no
; tensor or graph library to print JavaScript. See the Loop IR JavaScript
; backend design doc in .ai/.
;
; Wrapped false, with a [js_] prefix on every module: the mirrors (js/melange)
; copy the sources and refer to [Js_ast] unqualified, as the rest of the repo's
; mirrored libraries do. Depends on [fmt] only, and is JS-reachable from its
; first commit (js/melange/js_ast), so the integer rule applies: no printer
; arithmetic assumes a 63-bit [int], and no OCaml [int] is ever formatted into
; the output.

(library
 (name js_ast)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries fmt))
